A --base-url on a reserved name (.invalid, .test, .example, .localhost) now stops retrying after a DNS failure. It's committed as a4c72965 with "Fixes #1120"; I haven't pushed it. Format check, clippy with -D warnings, build and the full cargo test all pass.

Measured on the built binary with the probe from #1120:

| | Wall time | Exit | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| Before | 1m04s (six attempts) | 1 | the usual network error |
| After | 7.4s (only the library's own quick retries) | 1 | one new note, printed once |

The new note reads: `could not resolve nonexistent.invalid: it is a reserved name (RFC 6761) that can never resolve, so retrying cannot help. Check --base-url (now http://nonexistent.invalid/v1/chat/completions).`

What changed
• `src/prompt/reserved_dns.rs` (new): the note is only produced when the error is a DNS failure and the host is one of the four reserved names (or bare localhost). The match is on whole name parts, ignores case and allows a trailing dot. The module's opening comment gives the reason and points to @yuanhao's decision. no_retry_note() runs the existing loopback check first, then this one, so each of the two retry loops in prompt.rs makes one call.
• `loopback_refused.rs`: I made its existing url_host shareable and reused it rather than copying it.
• `prompt_retry.rs`: one comment line beside the retry classifier (TRANSIENT_ERROR_SHAPES) says reserved names fail fast and other DNS errors keep retrying.
• `tests/module_size.rs`: two size limits went up by one line each — prompt.rs for the new module line, prompt_retry.rs for the comment. The task listed three files; this was a fourth, and the file-size test required it.
• Docs: one paragraph in troubleshooting/common-issues.md, next to the existing loopback one.

Tests
• The fixture is the real error text I captured with --verbose, not a guess.
• An ordinary missing domain (yoyo-no-such-host-1120.com) is pinned by a table row as still retrying, which is the second test @yuanhao asked for. I did not run it live, since it takes over a minute by design.
• Other rows that must not trigger: example.com, invalidator.dev, notinvalid, mytest, a reserved host whose error is "connection refused" or a timeout, and an error with no URL.
• Positive control: forcing the reserved-name check to always say no made 3 of the 4 tests fail. The fourth passed only because it compared two empty results, so I added an assertion that the note is actually produced. The check was restored in the same command.

Not done: a DNS failure still gets no 💡 hint, because the hint code looks for "dns resolution failed" while the real error says "dns error", and prompt_retry.rs is at its size limit. #1120 will close when this is pushed, so I posted the fix and the real error text as a comment on #1086, which already tracks those hints.
